{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489193-you-can-climb-the-iron-throne","id":1489193,"title":"You CAN climb the Iron Throne","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-05T00:00:50-07:00","id":1489193,"title":"You CAN climb the Iron Throne","content":"Look...I've heard all the scary bullshit. We're the bad guys, the bogeyman, the anti-awakening. That's the crap the master's use, the same shit they pretend is held by the bad guys. They're holding on to the secrets they don't want you to know. How can we hold ourselves to a higher paradigm if that paradigm is limiting?!<br /> <br /> I've come to a very tentative/testing agreement with a member of the veil (read:he keeps trying to kill me)<br /> <br /> The only truth is that there's no existence but the one you make for yourself. When you look in the mirror, do you feel confident?<br /> <br /> There's true signs we can find for ourselves.<br /> <br /> BICHOP, proponent of reflection","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27517-theran","user":"Theran","date":".  Do you know what you believe? 08-05-2022, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27517-theran","name":"Theran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T05:45:29-07:00","id":1489223,"title":"","content":"Personal offense of the misunderstanding of the Guardians understanding and conception asides, you do realize the issue of discussion is a <i>bug</i>, not a <i>feature</i>, being sold as an incentive to those who saw the unfathomable and said &quot;Yep, I cannot fathom that.&quot;<br /> <br /> At some point in that path to godhood, you have to realize that is a undertaking that, at the end of the day, only ever needed you. Tyrant gods don't make other tyrant gods-they tolerate their losses against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T06:41:20-07:00","id":1489224,"title":"","content":"I'm so confused","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T07:13:46-07:00","id":1489226,"title":"","content":"Becoming a self made Tyrant means that, at the very least, archmage Ententes with Seer and Pentacle mages will try to stop you, since neither want the candidate to Ascend. The Exarchs only promote their favored servants to Lesser Iron Seals, they would not take kindly to someone trying to become an independent Tyrant. The mage who tries that will need to be very good in order to have the slightest chance of success. Even so, the Exarchs will only tolerate the loss, because after all, they have worked for thousands of years to reinforce their symbolic grip on the material. So unless the upstart does something truly revolutionary, the Iron Throne still will be vastly more influential: &quot;Sure, you are the absolute ruler of a micro nation, but our empires span continents&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-05-2022, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T07:25:50-07:00","id":1489227,"title":"","content":"I assume the foremost is an argument about the value of the Seers of the Throne. The problem is that it makes the argument that ironically should lead one <i>away</i> from obeisance of the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Of course, the very nature of the Exarchs betrays the fact that it's always a suckers game to kneel to them. <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.fandom.com/wiki/Song_of_Maybe#What_is_Royalty?\" target=\"_blank\">Royalty is a continuous cutting motion</a>-if the heavens can be seized, why kneel to monsters when you can <i>seize the heavens</i>?<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Pentacle Orders ironically more truly embrace that notion while having the idea that there really ought to be some rules and order to these things.<br /> <br /> Usurpers don't want you realizing usurping is an option. It is the base folly of tyranny. That the Seers join those they think they can't beat betrays their own defeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T09:43:55-07:00","id":1489239,"title":"","content":"A seer wouldn\u2019t overthrow the Exarchs. He\u2019d just join them as a <i>new</i> Exarch. The old Exarchs aren\u2019t hoarding their power, it\u2019s just a Seer needs to prove his loyalty to <i>join</i> the overlords of the Supernal World. Why redesign the wheel by starting from scratch, when you can share in the power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T10:20:49-07:00","id":1489243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489193-you-can-climb-the-iron-throne?p=1489239#post1489239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A seer wouldn\u2019t overthrow the Exarchs. He\u2019d just join them as a <i>new</i> Exarch. The old Exarchs aren\u2019t hoarding their power, it\u2019s just a Seer needs to prove his loyalty to <i>join</i> the overlords of the Supernal World. Why redesign the wheel by starting from scratch, when you can share in the power?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've mentioned it before, and I'll say it again: it's important to note that adding Exarchs to the roster is a failure that the Exarchs make the best out of rather than any sort of success or evidence of the system working as intended. A Seer who realizes their potential to seize the heavens realizes that, to some degree, it's all them. The most succesful ones follow that realization all the way to Ascension. What the Exarchs do is try to obfuscate the reality of &quot;it's all them.&quot; They stretch the import of their involvement in the nurturing of that &quot;it's all them&quot; and diminish how much is &quot;it's all them&quot;. They try to make it look like they paved the way, and when that fails they work to make them believe that their attempts to keep them from the heavens was instead a way to truly ensure that they belonged with them, initiation rather than obstruction. Any Seer who joins the Exarchial Ranks will know, by the time attained, that it's all a Lie, but it is the right of the powerful to Lie like that, and know that they would do the same to the others if they had done the same.<br /> <br /> A Seer who imagines <i>loyalty</i> is what's going to earn their starry fields is a Seer who has accepted the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/904882-you-just-have-to-do-this-random-seer-rant#post904882\">Just</a> nature of their gods, and serve only as a stepping stone for others who will play both sides of the Exarch's truths to get what they want. The rising stars of the Tyranny of the Defeated are those who are not <i>that</i> terribly loyal to the defeat it's gods espouse.<br /> <br /> If the Exarchs had their way, no one would raise their head, let alone do something as galling as <i>join them</i>. The wheel doesn't need to be redesigned, but it does grow in protest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-05-2022, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T10:31:42-07:00","id":1489244,"title":"","content":"I like your idea better! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T12:47:49-07:00","id":1489258,"title":"","content":"I think that, while the details of the end of the Time Before remain ambiguous, the position of the Exarchs does imply something uniquely empowering that ensures their primacy above other Supernal Gods or the Ascended, whether or not one imagines that to have been a literal Celestial Ladder.<br /> <br /> Seers may Ascend, and indeed mages of other affiliations do as well, but I think the lore of the setting and how it generally functions bears out that doing so does not manage to seize the heavens in the manner that the Exarchs did. The Corpus Author went up there and even changed something fundamental about the nature of magic, and yet the Lie still reigns over all.<br /> <br /> Under those circumstances, I do think the outlook of the Seers maintains a certain logic, that even to Ascend on their own would not place them near the heights of the Thrones. I think a Seer could even make an argument that even in the event that Ascension in service to the Exarchs is no easier or more frequent than doing so by any other means or motives, the end result is still being an Ascended being who is part of the system that resides in the Supernal that holds supremacy over reality. And I think if one is of the mindset to be a Seer, they can see greater value in even being a small component of the encompassing essence of &quot;all human endeavours end in futility&quot;, compared to somebody such as Merlin sitting upon a cushion of the legend of Camelot.<br /> <br /> I could see the argument that anybody Ascending at all constitutes a failure state for the Exarchs, but I think the setting doesn't make that indisputable. I think details are presented that characters could organize into a genuinely reasoned argument that the Exarchs actually are in favour of some select people Ascending. Or perhaps it's not so much particular people as it is favouring those who would do so in ways that reinforce the primacy of their concepts. They don't care who you are as a person so long as your journey to Supernal existence entailed the tools of oppressive hierarchy and existential obliteration.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T13:30:31-07:00","id":1489263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489193-you-can-climb-the-iron-throne?p=1489258#post1489258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, while the details of the end of the Time Before remain ambiguous, the position of the Exarchs does imply something uniquely empowering that ensures their primacy above other Supernal Gods or the Ascended, whether or not one imagines that to have been a literal Celestial Ladder.<br /> <br /> Seers may Ascend, and indeed mages of other affiliations do as well, but I think the lore of the setting and how it generally functions bears out that doing so does not manage to seize the heavens in the manner that the Exarchs did. The Corpus Author went up there and even changed something fundamental about the nature of magic, and yet the Lie still reigns over all.<br /> <br /> Under those circumstances, I do think the outlook of the Seers maintains a certain logic, that even to Ascend on their own would not place them near the heights of the Thrones. I think a Seer could even make an argument that even in the event that Ascension in service to the Exarchs is no easier or more frequent than doing so by any other means or motives, the end result is still being an Ascended being who is part of the system that resides in the Supernal that holds supremacy over reality. And I think if one is of the mindset to be a Seer, they can see greater value in even being a small component of the encompassing essence of &quot;all human endeavours end in futility&quot;, compared to somebody such as Merlin sitting upon a cushion of the legend of Camelot.<br /> <br /> I could see the argument that anybody Ascending at all constitutes a failure state for the Exarchs, but I think the setting doesn't make that indisputable. I think details are presented that characters could organize into a genuinely reasoned argument that the Exarchs actually are in favour of some select people Ascending. Or perhaps it's not so much particular people as it is favouring those who would do so in ways that reinforce the primacy of their concepts. They don't care who you are as a person so long as your journey to Supernal existence entailed the tools of oppressive hierarchy and existential obliteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gods can be killed, or as least subjugated.&quot; and &quot;If you can't beat them, join them.&quot; are the pieces you're looking for to this &quot;puzzle.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing of the matter is that, for a cast who claims Tyrant as title, both of these are normal expectations. The other supernal gods seem different to the Exarchs because they operate on a principle of being that is more instrinsically &quot;harmonious&quot; (for lack of a better word) with other concepts-as-action-and-being. This thing that is &quot;Become Above All Else and Do Not Permit Challenge To Thus&quot; will naturally fight and employ imaginative measures against all things that would bear equal measure to it with a lot more initiative, nevermind questions of human agency being a mover beneath the tyrant-symbols. It is a thing that does not co-exist <i>lightly</i>.<br /> <br /> Likewise, as a thing that is concerned with assertion over others and everything, the fact that the problem of Awakening and Ascension happens no matter what, mixed in with all those inevitable problems that conception of Time and Fate bring in, means that the Exarchs not only have to accept that others will Ascend into the Heavens, but that they have/had/are-will have had always done so. If you can't <i>stop</i> contenders from winning, then you can at least settle for the who, how, why, and to what end of it. If you can't stop people from joining you, the least you can do is work to keep yourself <i>above</i> those who join the starry-eyed existence-definers.* If others can gain divinity, it's better to bend them into extant weapons subordinate to them than let them dare to imagine higher and freer forms.<br /> <br /> &quot;Power is a chain you wrap around yourself&quot; may be the unofficial tagline of Mummy, but it's also the underlying point of Awakening, and nowhere is that more apparent than when one understands existence in Awakening in a way that tries to accept the Exarchs. At every stretch of the way, the goal is the strangle and ensnare contenders at the lowest possible point the could otherwise rise against you to, to calcify and resist the ascendence of others as much as possible. That some manage to get as far as the mercy seat is just a consequence of the way the game is set up for the Exarchs-they can't perfectly <i>win</i>-but it's critical in understanding the Exarchs that the place where that seems wibbly, seems <i>disputable</i>, is <i>not</i> reflective of the nature or character of an entity defined by their floor of understanding being defined by power, and for whom the cieling of being is the loneliness of power over all else as a <i>good</i> thing.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs don't want peers. They aren't happy with the peers they have to deal with already. They contest against each other as much as they do aspirants of godhood.<br /> <br /> When the Exarchs give power, their end goal is to give you just enough to <i>stop you</i>, to hang you beneath their feet. They've accepted some will do so just under them, and that many more will be leagues below, but they will defy any who would equal or surpass them. Pretending the gods named Tyrant are interested in less is to trust the leopards to not eat your face.<br /> <br /> *It may, in fact, be the case the reality most mages experience is only the slice of infinity where the infinite fucking babies can maintain their infinite fucking cribs, all else and other forms of infinity having already fractally surpassed/surpassing them. That doesn't save you from the fact you are in where they shit-if anything, it's why their grip is so tight in the worlds you dwell in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T11:49:46-07:00","id":1489354,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I look at something like Signs of Sorcery, and I feel as though the current way the setting is being presented is one where it opts to be ambiguous about whether or not we should consider something like Seer apologism to be totally delusional. Maybe with one or two exceptions, such as it pointing out that even most Seers see faults in the argument that the Exarchs are omnipotent to the point of constantly making reality edits, but it reads to me as not coming down totally on the side of Seer arguments that reconcile observations with their ideology being complete bupkiss. I feel as though part of the intended existential horror of the setting is to face the possibility that a lot of things really are functioning as the Exarchs design and their position is quite secure.<br /> <br /> I would still agree with the idea that the majority of Seers who buy into the idea that this system is good for them are rubes, but for gameplay purposes I think it presents compelling possibilities to let the Seers hold a position that is not externally confirmed to have a lot of holes in it.<br /> <br /> That wouldn't be to say that the Exarchs aren't giving people power to chain themselves with so much as Seers making arguments that this is proactively desired by them rather than a protective adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T16:33:48-07:00","id":1489370,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't becoming an independent Tyrant require creating a new type of Tyranny that is not symbolically classified as a subset of an existing Iron Seal or one produced by a combination of them ? Ascension requires the archmage to define what kind of Truth symbol they will become via their Omens, so theirs would need to &quot;map out&quot; to something entirely new (or superior in the case of the insanely ambitious ones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-06-2022, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T00:50:25-07:00","id":1489400,"title":"","content":"Although I admit, now I'm considering an angle where even if the Exarchs have no reason to fear being overthrown, even if what could be considered their conscious minds is aware of that, it could be essential for them to act as though they do because that's part of the role and symbolism of tyranny.<br /> <br /> It gives me an image where some archmasters speculate on the point of whether such a thing constitutes a constraint on the nature of being Supernal as they are, or whether they would enthusiastically play the role because of how it reinforces them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T01:22:50-07:00","id":1489455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489193-you-can-climb-the-iron-throne?p=1489370#post1489370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't becoming an independent Tyrant require creating a new type of Tyranny that is not symbolically classified as a subset of an existing Iron Seal or one produced by a combination of them ? Ascension requires the archmage to define what kind of Truth symbol they will become via their Omens, so theirs would need to &quot;map out&quot; to something entirely new (or superior in the case of the insanely ambitious ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>This leans very much into the importance of the fallen world. The idea the Supernal rules over all is a Lie, possibly a lie which the Exarchs have to perpetuate as Istar says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although I admit, now I'm considering an angle where even if the Exarchs have no reason to fear being overthrown, even if what could be considered their conscious minds is aware of that, it could be essential for them to act as though they do because that's part of the role and symbolism of tyranny. </div> </div> </div>It is also possible that the Lie is neither Supernal nor Fallen, it is Abyssal and no amount of resonance between fallen and supernal symbology can affect it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, do Scelesti ever ascend and would an Archmaster with knowledge of the Abyss to rival that of the Scelesti be able to ascend while opposing the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-08-2022, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T03:02:22-07:00","id":1489461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489193-you-can-climb-the-iron-throne?p=1489455#post1489455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This leans very much into the important of the fallen world. The idea the Supernal rules over all is a Lie, possibly a lie which the Exarchs have to perpetuate as Istar says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It is also possible that the Lie is neither Supernal nor Fallen, it is Abyssal and no amount of resonance between fallen and supernal symbology can affect it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, do Scelesti ever ascend and would an Archmaster with knowledge of the Abyss to rival that of the Scelesti be able to ascend while opposing the Abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries from 1e's take was that Scelesci don't ascend. Aswadim, the Abyss-aligned Archmages, are specifically &quot;normal&quot; Mages who aligned themselves to the Abyssal portion of the Pax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T07:20:55-07:00","id":1489481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489193-you-can-climb-the-iron-throne?p=1489400#post1489400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I admit, now I'm considering an angle where even if the Exarchs have no reason to fear being overthrown, even if what could be considered their conscious minds is aware of that, it could be essential for them to act as though they do because that's part of the role and symbolism of tyranny.<br /> <br /> It gives me an image where some archmasters speculate on the point of whether such a thing constitutes a constraint on the nature of being Supernal as they are, or whether they would enthusiastically play the role because of how it reinforces them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, there's a certain expectation to how someone who redefined themselves with the iconography and connotations of Tyrant is going to be. &quot;Accepting of others grasping and wielding power equal to theirs&quot; is not a thing you'd find in that expectation.<br /> <br /> The end of the road of magic is the removal of the barrier between action and being. The difference between Wisdom 0 and Ascension is mostly a matter of which one is the horse to the other's cart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T21:06:21-07:00","id":1489994,"title":"","content":"One simple post pokes the ant-hill. Can you see the magnifying glass above you, or are you still scrambling to protect your colony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27517-theran","name":"Theran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T21:09:39-07:00","id":1489995,"title":"","content":"And now you all have brought the throne closer to yourself by considering how close you are to it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27517-theran","name":"Theran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}